# The golden corpus is byte-exact test data, not prose.
#
# `tests/roundtrip.test.ts` and `tests/engine-roundtrip.test.ts` compare against
# these files one byte at a time, and several of them exist precisely to pin a
# spelling the formatter disagrees with — an unevenly padded table, a nested
# blockquote kept on one line, a file that stops without a trailing newline.
# Reformatting them does not tidy anything: it deletes the difference under
# test and either breaks the suite or, worse, quietly narrows what it covers.
packages/core/tests/golden/

.claude/
